<p id="p2">Today, Apple announced that it will host an event it calls “Surprise and Shine” on September 9, 2026, at 10:00 AM Pacific Time. The company is expected to announce the iPhone 18 Pro line, the highly-anticipated iPhone “Ultra”, as well as new Apple Watches and potentially new AirPods and HomeKit devices.</p>
<p id="p3">The event will be streamed live globally on <a href="https://www.apple.com/apple-events/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apple’s Events page</a> as well as on <a href="https://youtube.com/@apple" rel="noopener noreferrer">YouTube</a> and in <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/apple-tv/id1174078549" rel="noopener noreferrer">the Apple TV app</a>. Some members of the media were invited to watch the event in person at the Steve Jobs Theater at Apple Park.</p>
<p id="p4">MacStories will be covering all the details of the event, so stay tuned and get ready for September 9.</p>
